      "id": "GENUS_SMUTSIA",
      "name": "Smutsia",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "African ground pangolins — two species of large, terrestrial pangolins found in sub-Saharan Africa. Temminck's ground pangolin is the most widespread African species, found across the continent south of the Sahara. The giant ground pangolin is the world's largest pangolin, reaching 1.4 m in length. Ground pangolins are primarily terrestrial, walking on their hind legs with their forelegs held away from the body. African pangolins are better studied than Asian species but remain threatened by local hunting and, increasingly, international trafficking to Asia.",
      "lineage": "African Pangolins",
